        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, thank you for referring this 71-year-old male patient, admitted on 29/03/2018 with an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray showed pulmonary hyperinflation without consolidation. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed hypoxaemic respiratory failure. Blood tests revealed mild inflammatory markers. He was treated with supplemental oxygen therapy, nebulised bronchodilators (salbutamol and ipratropium), systemic corticosteroids, and intravenous fluids. Vital signs and oxygen saturation were monitored closely throughout the stay. The patient responded well to treatment, with significant symptomatic improvement. He was discharged on 30/03/2018 with oral prednisolone taper and optimised inhaler regimen. Follow-up with respiratory outpatient clinic has been arranged. Please continue monitoring his COPD and adjust maintenance therapy as appropriate.</div>"
            },
